Difference Between Encapsulation and Abstraction

Encapsulation means keeping the data of a class private and accessing it 
through public methods. It helps to protect the data from direct access.

Example: In Instagram, our password, phone number, and private account 
information are protected. We cannot directly access or change this data. 
We use the settings and options provided by Instagram.

Abstraction means hiding the complex working of a system and showing only 
the important things to the user.

Example: In WhatsApp, when we send a message, we only type the message and 
click the Send button. We do not need to know how WhatsApp encrypts, processes
, and delivers the message in the background.

In simple words: Encapsulation protects the data, while abstraction hides the
complicated working
